    "created_at": "2016-09-06T17:52:05Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-09-06T17:52:05Z",
    "body": "I don't think it's appropriate to disable file name adjustments. A user agent should not act against the user's wishes by controlling what files on their computer are going to be named.\n\nIf you think there is a browser bug where the suggestions specified via download=\"\" are not honored (e.g. by appending \".txt\"), that's a separate issue where browsers have made a UX decision for their users because they believe it's more user-friendly, and not really something the standard can or should touch on. That kind of thing is better discussed in browser bug trackers.\n",
